What are Liquid Barium Zinc Stabilizers?
Liquid barium zinc stabilizers represent an advanced class of heat stabilizers used in PVC processing, combining barium and zinc salts with organic ligands in a liquid formulation. These innovative stabilizers have emerged as environmentally preferable alternatives to traditional lead-based systems, offering superior processing characteristics while meeting strict regulatory requirements. Their primary function is to prevent thermal degradation during PVC manufacturing by neutralizing hydrogen chloride gas emissions, which can cause polymer chain scission and material discoloration.

